  "tagline": "Multi-model data platform (SQL, objects, globals, vectors) with built-in interoperability, big in healthcare.",
  "description": "InterSystems IRIS is the successor to Caché: a single engine whose storage layer is a fast, sparse multidimensional array ('globals') projected simultaneously as SQL tables, objects and JSON documents. On top it bundles an integration engine, FHIR/HL7 tooling (IRIS for Health), embedded Python, columnar storage, sharding and, since 2024, vector search for RAG. That combination makes it dominant in hospital records and health information exchange, including Epic's Chronicles database. It ships as Extended Maintenance releases (2026.1 in March 2026) and quarterly Continuous Delivery releases (2026.2 in July 2026). The trade-offs are proprietary ObjectScript, opaque pricing and a niche talent pool.",
